# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values below, then run: python main.py --text
# (main.py loads .env automatically, keys are never committed if you keep .env out of version control)

# --- GROQ_API_KEY (LLM, free tier) ---
# 1. Go to https://console.groq.com
# 2. Sign up / log in (Google or GitHub login works)
# 3. Left sidebar -> "API Keys" -> "Create API Key"
# 4. Name it anything (e.g. "urdu-voice-agent"), copy the key (starts with gsk_...)
# 5. Paste it below. Free tier has generous rate limits, no credit card required.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- AZURE_SPEECH_KEY / AZURE_SPEECH_REGION (TTS, free tier) ---
# 1. Go to https://portal.azure.com and sign in (create a free Azure account if you don't have one,
#    no cost, may ask for a card for identity verification but the Speech free tier itself is $0)
# 2. Click "Create a resource" -> search "Speech" -> select "Speech" by Microsoft -> Create
# 3. Pricing tier: choose "Free F0" (500,000 characters/month free, resets monthly)
# 4. Pick a region close to you - remember it, you need it below.
#    IMPORTANT: use the short region CODE, not the display name, e.g. "eastus" not "East US",
#    "westeurope" not "West Europe" - the SDK rejects the display-name form.
# 5. After deployment: go to the resource -> "Keys and Endpoint" (left sidebar)
# 6. Copy "KEY 1" and the region code shown there (e.g. "eastus")
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=

# --- OPENROUTER_API_KEY (LLM, alternate models - Gemini/Gemma/DeepSeek/Claude) ---
# 1. Go to https://openrouter.ai, sign up (no credit card required for free-tier models)
# 2. Left sidebar -> "Keys" -> "Create Key"
# 3. Paste it below. Lets a business pick its LLM model from the Guardrails page dropdown -
#    see src/llm.py's LLM_CATALOG for the exact model list. Groq remains the default and
#    doesn't need this key; only required if a business selects a non-Groq model.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Supabase (Postgres database) - required, the app reads/writes all persona/FAQ/
# stock/session data here now, not local JSON files ---
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com, create a free project
# 2. Project -> Connect -> ORM tab: copy the pooled connection string twice -
#    DATABASE_URL uses the transaction-mode pooler (port 6543), DIRECT_URL uses the
#    session-mode pooler (port 5432, needed for Alembic migrations' session-level locks).
#    Fill in the real DB password in both (no square brackets around it).
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=

# 3. Project -> Connect -> API Keys tab: copy the Project URL, the "publishable" key,
#    and the "secret" key (newer Supabase projects use this pair, not the legacy
#    anon/service_role names). The secret key is server-side only.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Which business row this process serves - only matters once you have more than one
# business seeded; defaults to "default" if unset. See src/business_context.py.
DEFAULT_BUSINESS_SLUG=default
